--- title Protecting a value from change
--- about PROTECT makes a value refuse modification. It applies to a word
--- about slot, to an object's fields and to a series itself, and the
--- about three are separate: protecting the word that holds a block does
--- about not protect the block.

--- id protection/a-protected-block-refuses-appending
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2]
protect b
error? try [append b 3]
--- result
#(true)

--- id protection/the-failure-has-its-own-id
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2]
protect b
e: try [append b 3]
e/id
--- result
protected

--- id protection/asking-whether-a-block-is-protected
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2]
protect b
protected? b
--- result
#(true)

--- id protection/an-unprotected-block-is-not
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2]
protected? b
--- result
#(false)

--- id protection/unprotecting-lets-it-change-again
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2]
protect b
unprotect b
error? try [append b 3]
--- result
#(false)

--- id protection/a-protected-string-refuses-appending
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "ab"
protect s
error? try [append s "c"]
--- result
#(true)

--- id protection/a-protected-objects-fields-refuse-assignment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
o: make object! [a: 1]
protect o
error? try [o/a: 2]
--- result
#(true)

--- id protection/a-protected-word-refuses-assignment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
protect 'zz
error? try [zz: 1]
--- result
#(true)

--- id protection/protecting-shallowly-leaves-the-nested-block-open
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is the boundary /deep exists to cross, and the one that
--- note makes protection worth asking about twice.
--- code
b: [[1]]
protect b
error? try [append b/1 2]
--- result
#(false)

--- id protection/protecting-deeply-reaches-the-nested-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [[1]]
protect/deep b
error? try [append b/1 2]
--- result
#(true)
